            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About ProBrothers Construction Services</h2>
              <div class="post-faq">
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What types of construction services does ProBrothers offer?</h3>
                  <p>ProBrothers provides a full spectrum of residential construction services, including <strong>custom home construction</strong>, <strong>home additions</strong> (second-story, sunrooms, in-law suites), <strong>kitchen remodeling</strong>, <strong>bathroom renovations</strong>, <strong>basement finishing</strong>, <strong>mudroom build-outs</strong>, <strong>door and window installation</strong>, and <strong>exterior renovations</strong>. Every project is managed in-house from planning through final finishing touches, serving homeowners across Delaware County, Chester County, and the Greater Philadelphia area.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Why should I hire a professional construction contractor instead of doing it myself?</h3>
                  <p>Professional contractors bring licensed expertise, access to quality materials, and accountability to local <strong>Pennsylvania building codes</strong>. DIY work on structural projects — additions, basement finishing, window replacement — risks costly permit violations, poor energy performance, and safety issues that can lower your home's value. ProBrothers' team manages permits, timelines, and inspections so you get a finished project that's built to last.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>How much does a custom home addition typically cost?</h3>
                  <p>Home addition costs in the <strong>Media, PA and Delaware County</strong> area vary widely by scope. A single-room addition typically runs <strong>$80,000–$150,000</strong>, a second-story addition <strong>$150,000–$350,000+</strong>, and a sunroom or enclosed porch <strong>$30,000–$80,000</strong>. Exact pricing depends on square footage, materials, structural complexity, and permit requirements. ProBrothers provides transparent, itemized quotes with no hidden costs.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Do you handle permits and building inspections?</h3>
                  <p>Yes. ProBrothers manages all permit applications and required inspections as part of the project. Pennsylvania and Delaware County have specific requirements for structural additions, electrical upgrades, and plumbing changes. Skipping permits is a major risk — it can void homeowners insurance and make the project non-transferable during a home sale. We handle the paperwork so you don't have to.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What is the difference between a home renovation and a full custom construction project?</h3>
                  <p>A <strong>renovation</strong> restores or updates an existing space — replacing cabinets, refinishing floors, upgrading fixtures — while keeping the original layout intact. A <strong>custom construction project</strong> may involve structural changes: adding square footage, relocating load-bearing walls, or building an entirely new structure from foundation to roof. ProBrothers handles both, tailoring each approach to the homeowner's goals and budget.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>How long does a typical home addition take to complete?</h3>
                  <p>Timeline depends on project size and scope. A small room addition typically takes <strong>8–14 weeks</strong> from permit approval to final walk-through. A second-story addition can run <strong>16–30 weeks</strong>. Factors that affect the schedule include permit processing time (varies by municipality in <strong>Delaware County</strong>), material lead times, and weather. ProBrothers provides a project timeline at the start and maintains regular communication throughout.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Can ProBrothers incorporate smart home technology into a new construction or addition?</h3>
                  <p>Absolutely. <strong>Smart home integration</strong> — automated lighting, smart HVAC controls, built-in speakers, and security systems — is best planned during the construction phase, before walls are closed. ProBrothers works with your preferred smart-home provider or can recommend trusted local vendors who specialize in wiring and device integration during the build.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>What exterior renovation services do you provide?</h3>
                  <p>ProBrothers' exterior renovation services include <strong>siding and stucco updates</strong>, <strong>roofing repairs and replacements</strong>, <strong>porch and deck installations</strong>, <strong>entry door and window replacement</strong>, and <strong>landscaping improvements</strong>. Exterior work not only improves curb appeal — it protects your home from the Mid-Atlantic climate's freeze-thaw cycles and heavy rain. All exterior work is done with weather-resistant materials appropriate for the <strong>Pennsylvania region</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>How do I choose the right construction company in Media, PA?</h3>
                  <p>Look for a contractor with: a verifiable portfolio of completed residential projects; proper <strong>Pennsylvania Home Improvement Contractor (HIC) licensing and insurance</strong>; transparent pricing with a detailed written quote; and a clear communication process. ProBrothers has served Delaware County and Chester County homeowners for 15+ years, with an in-house team (no subcontracting of core work) and a track record of on-time, on-budget delivery.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="post-faq__item reveal">
                  <h3>Does ProBrothers serve areas outside of Media, PA?</h3>
                  <p>Yes. ProBrothers serves homeowners across <strong>Delaware County, Chester County, and the Philadelphia metro area</strong>, including West Chester, Glen Mills, Kennett Square, Malvern, Springfield, Phoenixville, King of Prussia, and neighborhoods in Philadelphia itself. They also serve select communities in <strong>Delaware</strong> including Rehoboth and Greenville. Contact the team to confirm availability for your specific location.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
